3.1.text:
Article 27

1. For the purpose of recovery, women and children victims, witnesses and perpetrators of violence may obtain services from:a. Social institutions (groups or institutions that have scope in women and children) and or;
b. Social workers (Individuals who have competence to carry out recovery or rehabilitation) namely:
1. Nurses
2. Health workers
3. Counseling workers (2) What is meant by providing recovery services carried out by social institutions as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a is as follows:a. volunteer assistants make efforts to:
1. build equal relationships with victims so they are willing to open up in expressing their problems;
2. empathize and not blame victims regarding or related to their problems;
3. convince victims that no one may commit acts of violence;
4. ask what they want to do and what assistance is needed;
5. provide information and connect with institutions or individuals who can help overcome their problems; and/or
6. help provide information about legal consultation servicesb. spiritual counselors make efforts to:
1. explore information and listen to complaints from victims;
2. strengthen the faith and piety of victims and encourage them to carry out worship according to their respective religions and beliefs.
3. suggest solutions to domestic violence problems according to the victim's respective religion and beliefs.
4. provide understanding regarding equality between men and women.
3. What is meant by providing recovery services carried out by social workers as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b has the following provisions:a. explore victims' problems to help solve their problems;
b. restore victims from traumatic conditions through psychosocial therapy;
c. make referrals to hospitals or safe houses or service centers or other alternative places according to the needs of victims;
d. accompany victims in recovery efforts through assistance and counseling; and/ore. carry out resocialization so that victims can return to carrying out their social functions in society.

Article 3

The implementation of protection of women and children aims to:
a. ensure the fulfillment of the rights of women and children so that they can participate optimally in society in accordance with human dignity;
b. provide protection and provide a sense of security to women and children from all forms of violence and discrimination;
c. prevent and eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children including trafficking in persons;
d. provide services to women and children victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. empower women and children victims of violence.

Article 5

In implementing the protection of women and children, the Regional Government is obliged to:
a. establish basic policies for the implementation of protection of women and children in the Regional Action Plan;
b. implement policies for the protection of women and children established by the government and provincial government;
c. coordinate the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of the rights of women and children among regional apparatus organizations;
d. cooperate with other regions for the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of the rights of women and children;
e. strengthen institutional gender mainstreaming and mainstreaming of children's rights for the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of the rights of women and children;
f. establish P2TP2A in the Region;
g. ensure the implementation of excellent service in the protection of women and children, including for women and children victims of violence;
h. prepare a data system for the protection of women and children, including data on violence against women and children and.
i. establish UPTD PPA (Protection of Women and Children).

Article 16

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to receive:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. excellent service;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage; e. confidential handling;
f. psychological and legal assistance; andg. guarantees of rights related to status as a family member as well as a community member and the right to restitution.

REGENT OF PURWAKARTA,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of Violence;
b. that violence against women and children in the Region tends to increase, therefore the Regional Government and/or community need to play an active role optimally to provide protection, so that women and children are prevented and freed from violence or threats of violence, torture, or treatment that degrades human dignity and honor;
c. that protection of women and children is a mandatory concurrent affair which is the authority, obligation, and responsibility of the Regional Government, therefore regulation is needed as a basis for implementing comprehensive and integrated protection for women and children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children;

